        "title": "Financial Statement Analysis - Ratios and DuPont",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Ratio analysis turns the three statements into **comparable, dimensionless metrics** that\nlet you judge a firm against its own history, its peers, and benchmarks. Raw numbers are\nunitful and scale-dependent (a $10M profit means nothing without context); ratios normalize\nthem. They cluster into four families — liquidity, leverage, profitability, efficiency — and\nthe **DuPont decomposition** stitches profitability into a single causal tree."
    }
